WEBVTT

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.460
Super Popular Catcher
Licky-Licky

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.540
Yes!

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.520
Licky-Licky
Licky-

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.530
Good, good! Good, good!

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.390
I used up the rest of my
allowance for this month!

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.270
I'm no good at anything I do.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.730
Here.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.560
For you.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.960
Lost

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.080
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.010
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.880
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.260
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.970
Found

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:24.180
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.690
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.480
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.610
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.950
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.820
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.530
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.910
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.120
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.500
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.960
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.670
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.510
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.340
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.510
It's now or never

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.600
That is what they say

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.680
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.350
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.520
That is what they say

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.690
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.190
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.400
That is what they say

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.820
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.970
Licky-Licky's Trap

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.730
I, Ana, think there are different types
of Orpheus Rings, aren't there?

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:51.560
Yes, I'm surprised as well.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.320
I'm examining what's left of
the earring for specifics.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.270
More to the point,

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.330
makin' an amateur use
somethin' like that...

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.240
Who are these "Orpheus Order" fools?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:09.250
Well, they said they "embrace
the great Orpheus,"

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.680
"and seek to free man from the yoke
of the lesser gods," right?

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.350
Gods...

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.230
Yoke...

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.220
That's right.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.220
"The clarity of the human mind was
shunned by the gods,"

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.810
"and its fundamental abilities sealed."

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.870
That is the ideology that has continued,
unbroken, within that society.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:37.070
Such is the Orpheus Order.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.910
So, their objective is to
free those sealed abilities?

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.310
Yes,

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.580
and to restore man's "almighty power."

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.560
That's why they've reached out to Kaito?

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.670
To accomplish that?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.610
I don't know the details myself.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.090
But it's safe to say that whatever their reason,
it's no cause for celebration.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.650
The Orpheus Order appears to be

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:12.350
an even more radical organization than
the POG when it had lost its way.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.420
So, for the sake of your own greed,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.860
those guys are using puzzles
to bring about sorrow?!

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.550
Oh, no! I spilled it!

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.000
I told you, didn't I?

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.950
It's dangerous to try to
carry that much at once.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.650
I'm sorry.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.910
All right, we're gonna
clean this up, so move.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.930
I really am sorry, I'll help.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.880
Those guys!

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.860
Puzzle

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.720
What do you think you're doing?!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.390
You've got it wrong!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.790
What's wrong about it?!

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:50.970
It's true!

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.520
I was the one who said
I'd carry everyone's!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.020
Huh? Really?

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.250
Right now, the Puzzle
Club is training fiercely

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.280
to try to win the Junior Puzzle World Cup.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.270
They're even working
through their lunch hours.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.480
That's why I tried to
at least get their food.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.200
What are you saying?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.910
Airi, you're a member of
the Puzzle Club too, right?

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:19.540
I'm no good at either
making or solving puzzles.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.880
I really can't do anything at all, can I?

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.220
Oh! I have to go buy everyone's drinks.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.050
Well, Uppperclassman Nonoha,
if you'll excuse me!

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.410
Let me know if you get in trouble.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.480
I'll help you!

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.590
Thank you very much.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:43.120
Ow...

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.460
Are you okay?!

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.510
I'm used to it.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.280
I fell again...

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.550
At this rate, maybe you won't even
be able to remember.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.650
Me, that is.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.720
So, I've met him before?

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.660
When? Where?

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.340
All-Japan Elementary School
Puzzle Tournament, Division Series
2nd Place

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.940
I'm no good the way I am now.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.500
Is that so?

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:38.870
If you ask me, you're a
little too kind, that's all.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.500
It's not that you lack skill.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.250
It's just tucked away inside your heart.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:55.740
This ring is a charm.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:00.020
It can bring out your true power.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:05.730
Power tucked away inside my heart, huh?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.300
The cross sum too?!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.280
Cross Sum: Takeda's Puzzle
Airi Cleared

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.760
Not possible!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.560
The number area too?!

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.540
Number Area: Takeda's Puzzle
Airi Cleared

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.020
Not the number area!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.020
The block split too?!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.000
Block Split: Takeda's Puzzle
Airi Cleared

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.640
What, the block split?!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.570
I..I don't believe it!

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.980
The puzzles that Mr. Naoki himself made

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.840
for the Junior Puzzle Word Cup,

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.770
Aizawa solved in no time flat!

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.270
So sorry.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:57.440
I've shown you what
I'm really capable of!

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:58.790
Airi, that's so...

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.540
...incredible.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.580
You're incredible, Airi!

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:14.000
Yeah, yeah, Airi, Airi!

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.000
Oh, Mr. Takeda!

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.080
Yes?!

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.350
I'm  thirsty.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.920
Ma'am!

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.870
Here's your favorite, Miss Airi:

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.890
canned sweet bean soup.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.110
Hey! Why is this strained?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.260
Sweet bean soup should have
the beans still in it!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.910
Ah! I'll buy another one right away!

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.370
Jeez, he's just useless..

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.660
Airi?

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.620
Upperclassman Nonoha!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:46.860
What's going on?

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.810
That's what I want to ask.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.300
What's going on with you, Airi?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.460
Nothing at all.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.300
I've simply stopped
hiding who I really am.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.640
Who you really are?

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:02.970
Oh, it's perfect timing!

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:05.470
Upperclassman, can I ask you a favor?

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.490
Whisper, whisper, whisper,
whisper, whisper...

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:08.400
Huh?

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.870
I mean, that's what you said, right?

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.320
To let you know if I get in trouble.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.080
Unbelievable...

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.040
It's like it was a bad
dream or something.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.800
Still, friggin' Nonoha sure is late!

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.590
She's the one who asked to meet
so I could try her new sweets.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.730
That Airi...

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.630
I wondered what she meant
by "in trouble," but...

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.650
That girl...

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.800
Up?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:23.230
Jeez, how long are you gonna
make me wait, Nonoha?!

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:38.190
Kaito Daimon, Miss Airi seems to
want something from you!

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.200
Huh?

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.180
To Upperclassman Kaito
Airi

00:10:56.780 --> 00:11:00.970
What the heck is Airi up to,
inviting me to a place like this?

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.830
Upperclassman Kaito!

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.970
Airi?

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:11.160
Up till now, I've been a clumsy doofus,
no good at all,

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.980
but as of today I'm no longer that Airi.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:18.640
And so, I'll have you help as well.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:19.990
H..Help?

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.490
Kaito Daimon, you will tackle my puzzle!

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:27.200
What?!

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.260
Huh?

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:48.840
Kaito Daimon, you will tackle my...

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:49.830
Huh?

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:50.850
Um...

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.860
Why have I gotta go up against you?

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:58.370
It's obvious.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.620
If I beat you with my puzzle, no one can

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.740
make fun of me anymore, can they?

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.200
No one's makin' fun of you.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.680
Upperclassman Kaito,

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.750
if you don't accept my challenge,

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.630
something dear to you could get hurt.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.480
Something dear?

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:38.830
What do you think is
inside that stuffed doll?

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.150
You...

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.490
That!

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.920
It's an Orpheus Ring!

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:54.570
So, they've brainwashed Airi too!

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.180
It can't be!

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.600
You'll accept the challenge, right?

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:17.940
I'll present the puzzle on this computer.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.890
There's one Licky-Licky
block in the middle

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.350
of this five-by-five grid area.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:27.450
I'll put other blocks
around it to cover it up,

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.500
and you'll have to use the computer
to operate the crane

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:33.040
and remove the blocks in the way.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.020
Please rescue Licky-Licky

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.550
within the set number of moves.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.790
Simple, right?

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:39.920
However!

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.590
Each time you move the crane,

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.570
the Licky-Licky stuffed toy will

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:47.750
move closer to the ground.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:54.850
If you can't solve the puzzle within
the set number of moves...

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:08.440
What do you think?

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:11.200
Do you like my puzzle?

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.870
Dammit!

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.880
All right, fine.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.280
I'll save them, all of them.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.640
Puzzle time...

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.410
Let's begin!

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:41.150
You have just three moves.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:45.400
I may have shown a little too much skill!

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:47.930
But if I hadn't, it wouldn't be much of

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:50.160
a challenge for you, Upperclassman Kai-

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.460
I really get three turns, right?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:53.310
Huh?

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.160
Three!

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.340
Huh, huh?!

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:05.850
Two!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.550
Stop! Stop!

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.090
That puzzle just now was the wrong one.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.670
This is the real one.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:17.060
Huh?! You can't do that!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.930
Yes, I can.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.020
You get three turns this time.

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:29.700
Where am I?

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:35.580
Three.

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:42.460
Two.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:46.700
Th..This was the wrong one too.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.720
What, again?!

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:54.600
Hey, where I am I?

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.220
Let me out!

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.150
This is the next one.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:00.670
Three.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:01.560
Two.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.900
Gimme a break!

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:09.440
You seem out of your usual
element, Kaito Daimon.

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.320
Who are you?

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.630
But you may wish to hurry.

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:17.910
The Orpheus Ring places great strain
on the human mind.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.910
As you well know.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.760
That woman is speaking the truth, Kaito!

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:33.570
You two!

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:37.350
I realized it after I finished analyzing
the earring's remains.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:40.350
At this rate, Airi will be
swallowed up by the ring!

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:44.430
Furthermore, the ring is
made such that it cannot

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:45.980
be removed unless you win.

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:55.520
Now then, will you solve
this puzzle first?

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:59.250
Or will she be broken?

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:05.920
I want to beat Upperclassman Kaito.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:10.260
To win, and not have people
make fun of me anymore!

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:14.180
I will have my skills acknowledged.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.820
So... So...

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:32.400
Remove that many blocks
in just three moves?

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.400
That can't be solved!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.340
Airi!

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:44.640
This is bad!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.500
If the Giver loses consciousness,

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.940
the puzzle can't be repealed!

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.330
At this rate...

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.230
What will you do, Kaito?

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:03.270
Kaito!

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:08.800
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.080
Kaito!

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:27.040
Solved it!

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.780
I get it!

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:47.040
He's moving multiple
blocks with each turn.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.580
That's Kaito all right!

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.280
Look after Airi!

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.760
The hell is this?!

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.780
It ain't Nonoha...

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:06.320
It's your prized Galactic Puzzle Policeman,
Poly Cube.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.750
Hngraaa!

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:18.210
Monster & Hero Show

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:27.160
No..Nonoha, you...

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.160
I'm Tebero.

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:33.170
Te..Tebero?

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:43.790
Thanks to you, I've collected
some splendid data.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.930
Thank you, Nonoha Itou.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.290
Huh?!

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:52.070
That person did that to
you, Upperclassman Nonoha?

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:54.480
I didn't ask for that at all!

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:56.850
I just wanted you to go to class for

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.480
something you'd forgotten.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.070
I know.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:01.490
Don't worry about it.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:05.240
Everyone's got something
they keep inside them.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.750
What I hate is those guys,

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:11.250
who would pull it to the
surface and use it for evil.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.680
No matter what they do to me,

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:17.250
I'd never want you to be used like that,
Upperclassman Nonoha.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:19.250
Thank you.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:26.090
Well, I guess I was a
little careless too.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.360
Still, when you heard "something dear"...

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:31.890
Kaito, is that what you think of me?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:33.300
No way!

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.040
When I saw that stuffed toy thing,

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:37.150
I thought of you, that's all.

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:38.240
Huh?

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:42.580
Say, I don't have that
eccentric of a face, do I?

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:45.400
I sure do love Licky-Licky!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.160
So you're not denying it?

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.560
It's oddly cute...

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:51.850
Huh? Oddly?

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.020
You'd say "oddly" about me?

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:54.270
You're just plain odd.

00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:55.370
Odd?!

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:57.900
Sweet Bean Soup

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:57.920
A-hem, o-hem!

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.760
This is the sweet bean soup
we have for you today!

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.730
We have not just bean but also chestnut

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:05.010
and pumpkin paste varieties!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:06.760
Look, I don't need these anymore.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:09.410
In that case, give us your next order...

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:11.010
Miss Airi!

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.690
Airi... Airi... Airi...

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:16.650
Upperclassman!

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:18.880
There now, there now...

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:21.980
Ai..Ai..Ai..Ai..

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:24.050
Miss Airi!

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:29.230
Leave me alone!

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:06.050
Is it at last my turn to appear, big sis?

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:09.630
Um, you're from the
Orpheus Order, Miss...

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:11.010
Melancholy!

00:24:11.010 --> 00:24:13.630
And I'm the cutest girl
there's ever been.

00:24:13.630 --> 00:24:14.640
Hey, now!

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:16.590
I can't let you get away with this.

00:24:16.590 --> 00:24:17.910
I challenge you!

00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:20.430
If you come for me, you'll
find yourself losing.

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.600
Cube, you're up!

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:26.670
Night of the Knights

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:25.010
Next time, "Night of the Knights"

00:24:25.010 --> 00:24:27.160
Well, be seeing you!
